From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <dpaa1@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dpaa: FMan CC static-tree install (productive, M3-3b)

Forward-port of the FMan Coarse-Classifier (CC) static-tree silicon
programming path from the ask20 branch into the COMMON board patch stack
(built-in for default/vpp/ask via the FSL_FMAN_PCD config from patch 0092).
Re-anchors the ask20 CC-tree STATIC MURAM programming path (PR14c body +
0050 CONT_LOOKUP group-table/miss-AD wiring) onto the 0092 PCD subsystem +
0097 KeyGen base, adapted to the dpaa1 flat-C steering API
(dpaa_fman_caps.c) instead of the ask20 dynamic handle model. This is PR3
of the dpaa1 PCD forward-port closing M3-3b.

What this adds
--------------
- fman_pcd_cc.c (new, fsl_dpaa_fman.ko): the productive static installer.
  Defines struct fman_pcd_cc_tree (the private handle 0097's
  fman_pcd_kg_attach_cc() forward-references through <linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h>)
  and a per-port static-tree registry on pcd->cc_trees.
  fman_pcd_cc_static_install() encodes a normalised struct
  fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec into a MURAM match-key table + action-descriptor (AD)
  table + the tree group-table[0] CONT_LOOKUP entry per LS1046A RM 8.7.4.1,
  then registers the tree so it is torn down on unbind. The MURAM internals
  (fman_pcd_muram_alloc / fman_muram_offset_to_vbase, the latter NOT
  EXPORT_SYMBOL'd) stay inside this module — exactly the 0097 KeyGen idiom.
  fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy() reverses the teardown.

- include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h: publishes the neutral, big-endian-ready
  descriptor struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_{key,spec} + FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_* presence
  bits + FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS, plus the two static-install prototypes.
  The neutral struct lives in the public header so both fsl_dpa.ko (which
  owns the host-endian struct fman_cc_static_tree in dpaa_fman_caps.h) and
  fsl_dpaa_fman.ko can see it without a circular include.

- dpaa_fman_caps.c (fsl_dpa.ko): makes fman_cc_tree_install() /
  fman_cc_tree_destroy() productive. install() gates on
  FMAN_CAP_CC_EXACT_MATCH (BIT0) BEFORE touching MURAM (spec sec 3.5),
  translates the host-endian struct fman_cc_static_tree into the neutral
  fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec (host->FMan-BE conversion in dpaa_cc_key_to_hw()),
  resolves the PCD via fman_get_pcd(fm), and delegates to
  fman_pcd_cc_static_install(). Adds #include "fman.h" for fman_get_pcd().

- Makefile: adds fman_pcd_cc.o to the FSL_FMAN_PCD object list.

What this does NOT add
----------------------
fman_cc_tree_add_key()/remove_key() STAY -ENOTSUPP: the dynamic add/remove
lifecycle requires the FMan Host Command doorbell (FMAN_CAP_HC_DISPATCH),
which the Mono Gateway DK's loaded 210.10.1 QEF blob does not implement
(board reports caps = 0x17). Only the static install path is productive.
See spec sec 3.5 (HC-off hardware fact, PR13 2026-05-13).

Verified: native arm64 compile of drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/ and
.../dpaa/ with LOCALVERSION=-vyos is 0 warnings / 0 errors; fman_pcd_cc.o,
dpaa_fman_caps.o and both built-in.a archives build clean.

Spec sec 5.4.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <dpaa1@vyos-ls1046a-build>
---

patch-series-cleanup (2026-09-11): split. New file(s) below moved to
kernel/common/files/ as plain tracked source (a 'new file mode' hunk IS
the file's content, so tracking it directly carries no diff-drift risk
vs upstream); copied into place by ci-setup-kernel.sh before this
(now much smaller) patch applies. New files that moved:
  drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_fman_caps.c
@@ -23,7 +23,10 @@
 
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/string.h>
+#include <linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h>
+
 #include "dpaa_fman_caps.h"
+#include "fman.h"
 
 /* dpaa_fman_caps.force=<u32>
  *
@@ -186,10 +189,108 @@
  * today and gracefully degrade on ucode-106 silicon.
  * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 
+/*
+ * Translate one host-endian struct fman_cc_key into the neutral, BE-ready
+ * struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key the fman-side installer consumes.  A field
+ * participates iff it (or its mask) is non-zero; multi-byte fields are
+ * converted host->FMan-big-endian here so the silicon-programming layer can
+ * copy them verbatim into MURAM.
+ */
+static void dpaa_cc_key_to_hw(const struct fman_cc_key *k,
+      struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key *hw)
+{
+memset(hw, 0, sizeof(*hw));
+
+if (k->is_ipv6)
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6;
+
+if (k->ethertype) {
+hw->ethertype_be = cpu_to_be16(k->ethertype);
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE;
+}
+if (k->proto) {
+hw->proto = k->proto;
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO;
+}
+
+if (k->is_ipv6) {
+/* IPv6 addresses are already network-order byte arrays. */
+memcpy(hw->src_ip6, k->src_ip6, sizeof(hw->src_ip6));
+memcpy(hw->dst_ip6, k->dst_ip6, sizeof(hw->dst_ip6));
+/* Presence keyed on a non-zero address. */
+if (memchr_inv(k->src_ip6, 0, sizeof(k->src_ip6)))
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP;
+if (memchr_inv(k->dst_ip6, 0, sizeof(k->dst_ip6)))
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP;
+} else {
+if (k->src_ip || k->src_ip_mask) {
+hw->src_ip_be = cpu_to_be32(k->src_ip);
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP;
+}
+if (k->dst_ip || k->dst_ip_mask) {
+hw->dst_ip_be = cpu_to_be32(k->dst_ip);
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP;
+}
+}
+
+if (k->src_port) {
+hw->src_port_be = cpu_to_be16(k->src_port);
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_PORT;
+}
+if (k->dst_port) {
+hw->dst_port_be = cpu_to_be16(k->dst_port);
+hw->present |= FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_PORT;
+}
+
+hw->target_qband = k->target_qband;
+hw->hm_handle = k->hm_handle;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Productive static CC-tree install (spec sec 5.4).  Gates on
+ * FMAN_CAP_CC_EXACT_MATCH (BIT0) BEFORE touching MURAM per spec sec 3.5;
+ * on a board without it (mainline ucode 106) returns -ENOTSUPP so the
+ * flavor layer fails soft.  On the Mono Gateway DK the 210.10.1 QEF blob
+ * lights CC up (caps = 0x17), so this path is live there.
+ *
+ * Translates the host-endian static tree into the neutral fman-side
+ * descriptor and delegates the silicon programming to
+ * fman_pcd_cc_static_install() in fsl_dpaa_fman.ko (which owns the MURAM
+ * allocator).  add_key/remove_key stay -ENOTSUPP: they require the Host
+ * Command doorbell (FMAN_CAP_HC_DISPATCH), which the board's ucode does
+ * not implement.
+ */
 int fman_cc_tree_install(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id,
  const struct fman_cc_static_tree *spec)
 {
+struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec *hw;
+struct fman_pcd *pcd;
+u16 i;
+int err;
+
+if (!fm || !spec)
+return -EINVAL;
+if (!(dpaa_fman_get_caps() & FMAN_CAP_CC_EXACT_MATCH))
 return -ENOTSUPP;
+if (spec->num_keys > FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS)
+return -EINVAL;
+
+pcd = fman_get_pcd(fm);
+if (!pcd)
+return -ENXIO;
+
+hw = kzalloc(sizeof(*hw), GFP_KERNEL);
+if (!hw)
+return -ENOMEM;
+
+hw->num_keys = spec->num_keys;
+hw->miss_qband = spec->miss_qband;
+for (i = 0; i < spec->num_keys; i++)
+dpaa_cc_key_to_hw(&spec->keys[i], &hw->keys[i]);
+
+err = fman_pcd_cc_static_install(pcd, port_id, hw);
+kfree(hw);
+return err;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_cc_tree_install);
 
@@ -208,7 +309,15 @@
 
 void fman_cc_tree_destroy(struct fman *fm, u8 port_id)
 {
-/* no-op stub */
+struct fman_pcd *pcd;
+
+if (!fm)
+return;
+if (!(dpaa_fman_get_caps() & FMAN_CAP_CC_EXACT_MATCH))
+return;
+pcd = fman_get_pcd(fm);
+if (pcd)
+fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(pcd, port_id);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_cc_tree_destroy);
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Makefile b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Makefile
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/Makefile
@@ -6,6 +6,6 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_FSL_FMAN) += fsl_dpaa_mac.o
 
 fsl_dpaa_fman-objs	:= fman_muram.o fman.o fman_sp.o fman_keygen.o
-fsl_dpaa_fman-$(CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD) += fman_pcd.o fman_pcd_kg.o
+fsl_dpaa_fman-$(CONFIG_FSL_FMAN_PCD) += fman_pcd.o fman_pcd_kg.o fman_pcd_cc.o
 fsl_dpaa_fman_port-objs := fman_port.o
 fsl_dpaa_mac-objs:= mac.o fman_dtsec.o fman_memac.o fman_tgec.o
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -256,4 +256,119 @@
  */
 void fman_pcd_kg_scheme_destroy(struct fman_pcd_kg_scheme *scheme);
 
+
+/*
+ * Static Coarse-Classifier (CC) install surface (spec sec 5.4).
+ *
+ * The dpaa1 CC steering API exported from the dpaa driver
+ * (fman_cc_tree_install() in dpaa_fman_caps.c) consumes a host-endian
+ * 5-tuple key/tree shape that is module-private to fsl_dpa.ko. To program
+ * the FMan CC silicon (which lives in fsl_dpaa_fman.ko alongside the MURAM
+ * allocator) without a circular include, dpaa_fman_caps.c normalises its
+ * host-endian struct fman_cc_static_tree into the neutral, already
+ * big-endian-ready descriptor below and hands it to the fman-side installer.
+ *
+ * A field participates in the match iff its mask word is non-zero. All
+ * multi-byte fields here are FMan big-endian (the dpaa-side translator does
+ * the host->BE conversion); the install body copies them verbatim into the
+ * MURAM match-key record.
+ */
+
+/* Bounds mirror FMAN_CC_MAX_STATIC_KEYS in dpaa_fman_caps.h (kept in sync
+ * by review; the install body re-checks num_keys against this).
+ */
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS	32
+
+/* Match-key field-presence bitmask for struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key.present. */
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE	BIT(0)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_PROTO		BIT(1)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_IP		BIT(2)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_IP		BIT(3)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_SRC_PORT	BIT(4)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_DST_PORT	BIT(5)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6		BIT(6)
+
+/**
+ * struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key - one normalised CC match key (FMan BE layout).
+ * @present:      bitmask of FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_* fields that participate
+ * @ethertype_be: L2 EtherType, FMan big-endian
+ * @proto:        L4 protocol (IANA), single byte
+ * @src_ip_be:    IPv4 source (BE) when !FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6
+ * @dst_ip_be:    IPv4 dest   (BE)
+ * @src_ip6:      IPv6 source (16 bytes, network order)
+ * @dst_ip6:      IPv6 dest   (16 bytes, network order)
+ * @src_port_be:  L4 source port (BE)
+ * @dst_port_be:  L4 dest   port (BE)
+ * @target_qband: qband to steer matching frames to (validated by caller)
+ * @hm_handle:    HM node MURAM handle to chain after match (0 = none)
+ */
+struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key {
+	u32 present;
+	u16 ethertype_be;
+	u8  proto;
+	u8  src_ip6[16];
+	u8  dst_ip6[16];
+	u32 src_ip_be;
+	u32 dst_ip_be;
+	u16 src_port_be;
+	u16 dst_port_be;
+	u16 target_qband;
+	u32 hm_handle;
+};
+
+/**
+ * struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec - a port's complete normalised static CC tree.
+ * @num_keys:    number of valid entries in @keys (0..FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS)
+ * @miss_qband:  qband for frames matching no key
+ * @keys:        evaluated in order; first match wins
+ */
+struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec {
+	u16 num_keys;
+	u16 miss_qband;
+	struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key keys[FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_MAX_KEYS];
+};
+
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_cc_static_install() - program a static CC tree into MURAM.
+ * @pcd:     PCD subsystem handle (fman_get_pcd(fm))
+ * @port_id: FMan port id (1..10 on LS1046A) this tree serves
+ * @hw:      normalised, BE-ready static tree spec
+ *
+ * Allocates a MURAM match-key table + action-descriptor (AD) table, encodes
+ * each key's CONT_LOOKUP AD per LS1046A RM 8.7.4.1, writes the tree
+ * group-table[0] entry, records per-port state on pcd->cc_trees, and returns
+ * 0. Re-installing on a port that already has a tree first tears the old one
+ * down (idempotent rebuild — the static/commit lifecycle). On any MURAM or
+ * validation failure no partial state is left installed.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success; -EINVAL bad args; -ENOSPC MURAM exhausted; -EBUSY
+ * concurrent install race.
+ */
+int fman_pcd_cc_static_install(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
+			       const struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec *hw);
+
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base() - fetch a port's installed CC tree MURAM base.
+ * @pcd:          PCD subsystem handle
+ * @port_id:      FMan port id whose installed tree to query
+ * @cc_muram_off: out param - RAW MURAM byte offset of the tree root (no >>4)
+ *
+ * The offset is suitable for writing into the BMI RX port FMBM_RCCB register
+ * via fman_port_set_cc_base() (board patch 0105) - the productive port-bind
+ * that points the silicon datapath at the installed static CC tree.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on success, -EINVAL on bad arguments, -ENODEV if no tree installed.
+ */
+int fman_pcd_cc_static_get_base(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
+				u32 *cc_muram_off);
+
+/**
+ * fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy() - tear down a port's static CC tree.
+ * @pcd:     PCD subsystem handle
+ * @port_id: FMan port id whose tree to remove. No-op if none installed.
+ *
+ * Frees the MURAM tables, unlinks per-port state, returns nothing.
+ */
+void fman_pcd_cc_static_destroy(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id);
+
 #endif /* __LINUX_FSL_FMAN_PCD_H */
